/target/
**/*.rs.bk
.env
/.claude/
*.priv.cbor
*.redb

# The hub's default key paths are relative (`./hub_operator.priv.cbor`,
# `./hub_exchange_custody.priv.cbor`, `./hub_escrow_secret.bin`), so the
# README's own quickstart -- `./target/release/hub ... --generate-keys`
# run from here -- writes all three into this directory. The two
# `.priv.cbor` ones are covered above. The escrow master secret was not,
# and it is the one docs/deployment.md §6.1 calls the one people
# underestimate: read it and you derive every escrow key ever handed
# out, which is what stopped a stolen `hub.redb` from being a stolen
# treasury. This repository is public.
hub_escrow_secret.bin
*.escrow_secret.bin
secrets/

.DS_Store
